{
  "requirement": "The harness MUST construct each assessment's mandatory input set by combining\nthe contributions specified by the requirements applicable to that subject and\nits inputs. A requirement that contributes inputs MUST cite this requirement and\ndefine which sources it contributes and when. The harness MUST include every\napplicable contribution, deduplicate identical selections, and report\nunresolvable mandatory inputs before inference. The complete set MUST be supplied\nin the initial model request.\nA file selected as a mandatory input MUST be visible under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.sources.local_provider`. A denied selection MUST abort\nunder {cite}`requirements.authoring.read_denial.mandatory`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I judge the tests adequate for `requirements.authoring.mandatory_inputs`. I did not request implementation source. The cited `requirements.sdk.sources.local_provider` and `requirements.authoring.read_denial.mandatory` were treated as context. Batch behaviour, nonzero exit status and usage records belong to `read_denial.mandatory` and were not reassessed.\n\n**Obligations and the tests that cover them**\n\n1. **Combine the contributions of the applicable requirements.**\n   - `src/authoring/inputs.rs#mod[tests]/fn[bundle_combines_direct_references_terms_and_current_existing_selectors]` checks the subject declaration, cited requirements (a cited `base` is included, a distant `distant` is not), term definitions, and the owning item of a `{test}` reference. It also checks that an `{impl}` item is not supplied, and covers an example as subject.\n   - `fn[only_edges_leaving_the_subject_contribute_inputs]` checks which edges contribute and which do not (citer, parent, helper, run).\n   - `fn[anchored_files_contribute_root_node_inputs]` and `fn[test_anchors_supply_only_the_selected_node]` check `:impl:` and `:test:` anchors, a whole file and a single node. The latter also checks that the sibling's text does not reach the prompt.\n   - `fn[references_contribute_their_owning_outline_nodes]` and `fn[generated_evidence_references_are_omitted_by_default]` check which reference sites contribute.\n   - `fn[mandatory_inputs_can_read_untracked_declarations_and_terms]` checks terms and untracked or staged sources.\n   - The citation-review and site-review inputs are checked in `src/authoring/mod.rs` by `fn[citation_reviews_use_their_prompt_and_record_the_item_and_citations]`, `fn[site_reviews_use_their_prompt_and_record_applies_and_the_site]` and `fn[book_commentary_reviews_supply_the_whole_passage_and_check_concordance]`.\n\n2. **Include every applicable contribution.** The tests above use exact-equality assertions (`assert_eq!` on the whole input list in `fn[anchored_files_contribute_root_node_inputs]` and `fn[unresolvable_earlier_inputs_do_not_block_reassessment]`, and on the input count in `fn[citation_review_inputs_combine_item_declarations_terms_and_built_ins_once]` and the site test). A dropped contribution would fail them.\n\n3. **Deduplicate identical selections.** `fn[citation_review_inputs_combine_item_declarations_terms_and_built_ins_once]` cites `ready` twice and `other` once. It has two requirements share one term, and gives the built-in `habeas:util` text twice. It asserts each appears once and that the total is 5. The bundle test's definition count of 2 covers mutually referencing terms. The CLI test `fn[ollama_cli_delivers_sources_records_fixme_and_keeps_usage_content_free]` asserts a repeated delivery is recorded once.\n\n4. **Report unresolvable inputs before inference.**\n   - `fn[unresolvable_mandatory_inputs_fail_before_any_model_request]` in `tests/authoring_cli.rs` ignores the declaration file. It asserts the command fails, stderr names the path, the model listener is never contacted, and the evidence file is unchanged.\n   - `fn[disallowed_mandatory_inputs_abort_preparation]`, `fn[unreadable_or_denied_anchors_fail_before_inference]` and `fn[mandatory_inputs_outside_the_project_still_abort]` check the abort at preparation. They use an ignored declaration, a missing anchor file, a missing anchor node, an ignored anchor, and an outside-project path. They assert `PermissionDenied` and the path in the message.\n   - `fn[evidence_anchors_and_aliases_follow_project_ignore_rules]` checks that gitignore rules apply to anchors and symlink aliases.\n\n5. **Visibility under `local_provider`.** The ignored-file tests above (`.gitignore` hiding the declaration, the terms file or an anchored file) and the outside-project test exercise this.\n\n6. **Supply the complete set in the initial request.**\n   - The citation test asserts the initial prompt contains the item hash, the requirement text and the built-in text.\n   - The site test asserts the subject message equals the template filled with `model_mandatory_inputs()`.\n   - The CLI test asserts the first request contains the requirement, the definition text and `fn ready_test()`, and does not contain the implementation.\n   - `fn[test_anchors_supply_only_the_selected_node]` checks the prompt text.\n\nEach obligation, including the failure cases the text names, has a test that runs the behaviour and asserts its outcome. I found no gap.",
  "references": "24022a85373a405b0fb3408b99edf1d1bbc96fd33788256d087c885bb430c4d7",
